From 09d515d7e30ab5e668d83269d33a723968e63a28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:56:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(multiaxis): swing the rotaries before the approach
 descent

The five-axis approach set the first station pose on the modal
builder and then pushed the Plunge to first contact, so the rotary
swing rode the descend. The approach now states the pose as its own
zero-travel rapid (a standstill rotary index on the hop plane, the
tip held) before the plunge, in contour_curve and in the stamp emit
loop for every posed kind. The builder keeps a zero-travel move whose
pose changed and the post solves it as a pure rotary reorientation,
so the swing always commands. Intermediate cut moves keep the modal
tilt law.

The law tests that read rapids and ball centres now read the
swing-free stream (no_swings/sans_swings helpers); a decision record
sits in docs/decisions/3414-approach-rotary-order.md.

Fixes #3414
