From acb9d8bc0ebe3a86e2a3ab44f5ffff23c5bb2fde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:14:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(multiaxis): swing the rotaries upright before an
 upright approach

The #3414 standstill swing ran only in the leaned arm of the stamp.
Both upright arms (the arc arm and the linear arm) stated an upright
pose directly on an air-to-cut move, so a rapid that travelled under
a lean handed the descent a 90-degree rotary turn: on multiaxis_rough
over the slab with a boss, move 261 turned back to upright while it
reached the part.

Both upright arms now emit the same zero-travel rapid when they are
reached out of air (in_air), the move is not a Rapid, and a held pose
exists and differs from the upright one. An opening upright move from
held_pose == None states the upright home as its own (#3300) and
swings nothing; a pose that already matches drops in the builder, byte
for byte as before. The ball only rises through the swing, so nothing
new is swept.

Pinned two ways: the_approach_rotates_before_it_descends now runs
no_pose_change_rides_the_air_to_cut_move over multiaxis_rough
(slab_with_boss) and contour5d, red at the reviewer's exact move 261
without the linear arm's swing; and the new stamp unit test
an_upright_arc_out_of_air_swings_at_a_standstill_first is red without
the arc arm's swing. The decision record cites onRapid and tilt()
for the posted rotary index, not the g93 feed branch.

