The merged #3300 law states the upright home on the opening move. The
app's rough ladder opens with a zero-travel Rapid (the plan's own first
move states no travel), so the stamp's opening statement is a
zero-travel Rapid with axis Some([0, 0, 1]). The no_swings and
sans_swings filters read it as a rotary index - a zero-travel Rapid
whose axis changes off no held pose - and stripped it, which desynced
the plain-vs-posed pairing in multiaxis_rough_peels_the_same_ladder_
and_poses_its_walls (the ball moved at 0).

A swing is a zero-travel rapid whose axis CHANGED; an opening upright
statement from held_pose == None is the home the path inherits,
commanded as zero angles, and no rotation happens. All three filter
copies (app no_swings, motion sans_swings x2) now keep it; a leaned
opening from no held pose still counts as a swing.

